WEBVTT

q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.259
Does hybrid execution collapse the whole graph, or can it preserve structure and choose child by child?

q0002
00:00:10.259 --> 00:00:20.983
This episode has one job: Hybrid and partial-hybrid modes differ in whether they collapse a whole subtree or preserve upper structure while dispatching selected children to packed or dense materialization.

q0003
00:00:20.983 --> 00:00:31.707
We build on CM-IR nodes, sharing, and roots, Packed truth vectors: big integers, machine words, and masks; their definitions stay fixed while this lesson adds a new layer.

q0004
00:00:31.707 --> 00:00:40.822
Hybrid can collapse an eligible region; partial-hybrid preserves more graph structure and dispatches selected children.

q0005
00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:49.937
Watch for the label hybrid materialization; it stays attached to the artifact this episode means.

q0006
00:00:49.937 --> 00:00:58.480
When we say partial-hybrid materialization, the highlight identifies its layer before we interpret it.

q0007
